{"passages": [{"reference": "8.6", "verdict": "accept", "checks": {"complete_coverage": true, "no_added_claims": true, "names_and_negations": true, "lexical_fidelity": true, "uncertainties_disclosed": true}, "findings": []}, {"reference": "8.7", "verdict": "blocked", "checks": {"complete_coverage": false, "no_added_claims": true, "names_and_negations": true, "lexical_fidelity": true, "uncertainties_disclosed": true}, "findings": [{"source_quote": "ἐάν γε πράττοντες τὰ διὰ Μωϋσέως .... ὃν ἠγνόησαν μὴ μισήσωσιν", "english_quote": "provided that, while doing the things through Moses .... they do not hate the one they did not know", "issue": "The draft faithfully preserves the verified printed gap and covers the surviving clauses. Nevertheless, the gap leaves source content and its precise syntactic contribution unavailable, so complete content-level coverage cannot be certified. The block concerns missing meaning, not ordinary interpretive ambiguity or an alleged OCR error.", "suggested_revision": "Keep the four-dot gap and the blocking disclosure. Context alone cannot authorize its restoration. Recovering missing content would require an explicitly evidenced and separately authorized source-level revision, distinguished from the supplied Lagarde reading; wording from another edition must not be silently inserted. Any resulting replacement requires fresh review.", "severity": "blocking"}]}, {"reference": "8.8", "verdict": "accept", "checks": {"complete_coverage": true, "no_added_claims": true, "names_and_negations": true, "lexical_fidelity": true, "uncertainties_disclosed": true}, "findings": []}, {"reference": "8.9", "verdict": "accept", "checks": {"complete_coverage": true, "no_added_claims": true, "names_and_negations": true, "lexical_fidelity": true, "uncertainties_disclosed": true}, "findings": []}, {"reference": "8.10", "verdict": "revise", "checks": {"complete_coverage": true, "no_added_claims": true, "names_and_negations": true, "lexical_fidelity": true, "uncertainties_disclosed": false}, "findings": [{"source_quote": "μήτε ἐνὶ τόπῳ ἀποκεκρυμμένον", "english_quote": "is not hidden in a single place", "issue": "The supplied print has smooth-breathing ἐνὶ, whereas the numeral's usual dative is ἑνί. The printed form also admits the extended preposition ἐνί, yielding 'in a place.' The contextual numeral/locative interpretation behind 'in a single place' is defensible, but the draft does not disclose this printed-form decision, preserve the prepositional alternative, or explain its preference. This is an orthographic and lexical disclosure issue, not evidence of OCR corruption.", "suggested_revision": "Add a note quoting the supplied ἐνὶ exactly. Compare the prepositional reading 'not hidden away in a place' with the numeral/locative interpretation 'not hidden in a single place,' explaining how the contrast with universal readability supports the latter. Distinguish any proposed normalization to ἑνὶ or expansion to ἐν ἑνὶ from the supplied reading rather than silently correcting it. The revised wording and disclosure must undergo fresh review.", "severity": "major"}]}]}
